        "url": [
          "https://www.robeuk.com/our-stories/bruno-poet-shaping-light-story-and-the-space-between",
          "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.11792"
        ],
        "timestamp": ["2026-10-07", "2026-10-08"],
        "note": "Suggests that AI can support iterative lighting cue generation but foundational human understanding is key."
      }
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Cross-source insight: Both professional designers and AI research agree that lighting must be driven first by story and space before tools or technology, pointing to human artistic intent as the foundation onto which AI assistance should build.",
      "Limitation: Current AI lighting design systems are trained on limited, style-controlled datasets and lack broad evaluation benchmarks, making their real-world applicability and generalizability a key unresolved challenge."
    ]
  }
